⏺ What's left when you're ready                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                         
  Required: the push (3 commands)                                                                                                                                        
   
  git push --force-with-lease origin main                                                                                                                                
  git push origin :refs/tags/v1.9.0                                                                                                                                    
  git push origin v1.9.0                                                                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                                                       
  That's it. Run them in order, in this repo.                                                                                                                            
   
  Pre-push, on GitHub                                                                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                       
  Branch protection on main. If you have rules requiring linear history, signed commits, status checks, or blocking force-pushes, the first command will fail. Quick     
  check before pushing: GitHub repo settings → Branches → check rules on main. If force-push is blocked, temporarily disable that rule, push, re-enable. Couple of
  clicks.                                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                                                       
  If you've never set up branch protection on this repo, this is moot.                                                                                                   
   
  After the push                                                                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                                                                       
  Other local clones (your other machines). Any clone that fetched between Apr 10 and now has the old chain. To bring them in line:                                      
   
  git fetch origin                                                                                                                                                       
  git reset --hard origin/main                                                                                                                                           
  git tag -d v1.9.0
  git fetch origin tag v1.9.0                                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                       
  GitHub release. GitHub auto-regenerates the v1.9.0 release tarball from the new tag tree. Nothing to do — it just happens. If you manually attached files to the v1.9.0
   release page, those persist.
                                                                                                                                                                         
  Separate decision: cut v1.9.1?                                                                                                                                         
   
  The history rewrite cleans source. The published binaries at v1.9.0 are immutable in their respective registries:                                                      
                                                                                                                                                                       
  - npm prismcast@1.9.0 — past the 72-hour unpublish window. Cannot recall.                                                                                              
  - ghcr.io prismcast:1.9.0 — could republish, but anyone who already pulled has the old digest.                                                                       
  - Homebrew tap formula — auto-picks up the fix from the regenerated GitHub tarball on next brew upgrade.                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                         
  If you want the leak gone from artifacts users actually install, cut a v1.9.1 with the fix and treat v1.9.0 as superseded. If you're OK with the artifact leak         
  persisting (the source is clean, the issue is cosmetic for downstream users since the comment never affected behavior), do nothing. Your call.                         
                                                                                                                                                                         
